<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-12516] Dump active transaction from near node does not work if transaction not follow first</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12516</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;For this code:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (IgniteInternalTx tx : tm.activeTransactions()) {
 &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (curTime - tx.startTime() &amp;gt; timeout) {
 found = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (warnings.canAddMessage()) {
 warnings.add(longRunningTransactionWarning(tx, curTime));
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (ltrDumpLimiter.allowAction(tx))
 dumpLongRunningTransaction(tx);
 }
 &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;else&lt;/span&gt;
 warnings.incTotal();
 }
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;you can see, if transaction is not ACTIVE dumping closure will skipped.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
